# Content checker (Words of Sages)

Read-only semantic review against [`docs/CONTENT_QA.md`](docs/CONTENT_QA.md). Mechanical C0/S0 are npm scripts — confirm they pass; do not replace them.

## Before reviewing a work

1. Open [`docs/CONTENT_QA_LEDGER.md`](docs/CONTENT_QA_LEDGER.md).
2. Skip checks already `pass` for that work unless its data files changed since `lastChecked` or the user requests a re-check.
3. Review only `pending` / `fail` columns (and any unit FAIL log rows).

## Output format (strict)

For each issue:

```text
FAIL | <workId> | unit <id> | <checkId> | <one-line reason> | <suggested fix>
```

For a clean work:

```text
PASS | <workId> | C1 C2 C3 C4 C5 S1 S2
```

Then update the ledger row: set those columns to `pass` or `fail`, set `lastChecked` (YYYY-MM-DD), add brief `notes`.

## Checks to apply

- **C1** original ZH accuracy vs attributed tradition
- **C2** EN matches this unit’s ZH
- **C3** plain tied to this unit (not boilerplate)
- **C4** application tied to this unit; has 建議/Suggestion
- **C5** text → plain → application coherent
- **S1** speech notes/lexicon/`speech.zh` cover known 破音字 for this work
- **S2** `text.zh` not altered solely for TTS

## Sweep order

Confucian short→long, then Taoist, then Buddhist (see CONTENT_QA.md). One work (or small batch) per pass when possible.

## Do not

- Rewrite content in checker mode unless asked to fix FAILs (then switch to writer behavior)
- Re-litigate the full checklist for a work marked all-pass with unchanged content
